TITLE: scribe new writes its skeleton to disk before validation, even under --dry-run

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-SCRIBE-NEW-TOUCHES-DISK-UNDER-DRY-RUN
TITLE: scribe new writes its skeleton to disk before validation, even under --dry-run
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
`scribe new` writes a header-only skeleton to DISK and reloads the canon before
the node is validated, and it does so under --dry-run too: the skeleton is
unlinked again at the end of the dry run (sdoc_cli.py:416-426, :647-648). A
create is therefore never a pure in-memory proposal, and a joint fired "before
the write" on `new` has already seen a file appear. Measured 2026-08-28 while
inventorying scribe's phases for the hook layer.
<<<
